    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by the core tandem of **Gunnar Henderson** (78.49) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (75.59). **Gunnar Henderson** is our premier play, capitalizing on a significant dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) against Yesavage, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** draws a high-value matchup against Young (4.75 xERA) that optimizes his xwOBA profile. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) also emerges as a high-leverage start, benefiting from the same exploitable matchup against Kelly. While **Kyle Tucker** (51.25) carries a lower score due to an unfavorable matchup against Detmers, his elite base projection keeps him in the mix, though we are closely monitoring the impact of the pitcher's skill on his output.\n\nStrategic focus shifts to our speed-first utility strategy, where **Nasim Nunez** (63.18) earns a start despite hitting ninth. By leveraging his switch-hitting versatility and exploiting a favorable pitcher delivery time that enhances his stolen base probability, he provides the necessary category scarcity coverage we demand. The most difficult roster decision today involved **Josh Jung** (46.02), who narrowly missed the cut. While he offered better baseline talent than some starters, his matchup against the tough southpaw Messick and a lower overall efficiency score relative to our current infield configuration relegated him to the bench. We remain cautious regarding **Andy Pages** (49.46) and **Liam Hicks** (47.37), both of whom are projected as marginal plays; we will prioritize their efficiency to avoid unnecessary depletion of our remaining daily game caps.",
